## Methods
this is the syntax of declaring a method:
```C#
accessIdentifier static returnValue methodName(para){
    statiement;
} 
```

## default parameter
c# method allows user to define the default value like this:
```C#
static void HelloWrold(int a = 5){
    ...
}
```

## Named arguments
when executing the method, user can send arguments with `key: value` syntax:
```C#
static void HelloWrold(int a, int b){
    ...
}

static void Main(String[] args){
    HelloWorld(a: 1, b: 2)
}

```

## method overloading
with the method overloading, multiple methods can have the same name but different parameters:
```C#
static void Print(String a){
    Console.WriteLine(a);
}
static void Print(int a){
    Console.WriteLine(a);
}
static void Print(double a){
    Consoel.WriteLine(a);
}
```